            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The invention refers to a liquid polymeric composition comprising: (a) from about 2 to about 20 weight percent of a polymer; (b) from about 5 to about 40 weight percent of a radiopaque molecule with a molecular weight below 2000 g/mol; and (c) from about 40 to about 93 weight percent of a non-physiological solvent or solvent system; wherein (i) the sum of the weight percent of all components in the composition is 100, (ii) the polymer and the radiopaque molecule are not covalently bound and are both dissolved in the non-physiological solvent or solvent system, and (iii) the polymer is soluble in the non-physiological solution and insoluble in a physiological solution at room temperature, and (iv) the liquid polymeric composition is capable of forming, upon contact with physiological conditions, a radiopaque precipitate which maintains at least 50% of its radiopacity during at least 30 minutes and loses at least 50% of its radiopacity in less than 6 months.</p>
            </abstract>
